SUMMARY:Exploring Mount Nemo
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/mt-nemo-fall-26)**\n**Moun
 t Nemo is one of the best parts of the Niagara Escarpment and it's only a 
 short drive from the city!**\nWe'll follow the Bruce Trail for about 7 km 
 along the top of the ridge\, through old forest that grows right up to the
  cliff’s edge. Within a few minutes\, while immersed in this UNESCO bios
 phere reserve\, Toronto feels a lot further away than it is.\nThis isn't a
  simple stroll but it is accessible for anybody wanting to get into hiking
 . The ground is broken up in the best way\, with rock\, roots and the odd 
 scramble\, and the route keeps changing character as we go.\nNovember is a
  good month to do it. The trail is quieter than in peak fall colour season
 \, and depending on the year some leaves may still be hanging on. Most peo
 ple arrive not knowing anyone\, and by the time we're back at the cars you
 'll likely have a few new trail friends.\n**Accessibility**\nWilderness Un
 ion is committed to making our adventures as accessible as possible. If yo
 u wish to make an accommodation request relating to a disability or provid
 e feedback\, please do so by sending an email to info@wildernessunion.com\
 n**Highlights**\n**Close to the City:** It's an hour drive from Toronto\, 
 which makes this one of the easiest ways to get onto the escarpment.\n**Vi
 ews:** Whatever colour is left in the forest\, set against the dark green 
 of the cedars. Bare branches also mean longer sightlines across the valley
 .\n**Meet Your Crew:** A day on the trail with fellow members of the WU cr
 ew\, and a few new people to plan the next hike with.\n**Itinerary**\n**10
 :00** \\- Shuttle leaves from near Keele Station\n**10:00 - 11:00** \\- Dr
 ive to trail head\n**11:00 - 15:30** \\- Hike the trail with a stop for lu
 nch along the way\n**15:30 - 16:30** \\- Drive back to Toronto\n**Event co
 st: $55+HST. $40 optional transport also available. Please register [here.
 ](https://www.wildernessunion.com/adventures/mt-nemo-fall-26)**\n**About W
 ilderness Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoo
 rs community that connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors 
 and helps you find your people.\nMembers range from 20-40 years old. The g
 roup is a mix of GTA locals and newcomers to Toronto from within Canada an
 d abroad.\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our actual event att
 endance - we typically have 15-20 community members at each event. Large e
 nough that there's someone new to meet but small enough that it's not over
 whelming!\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.com](https://
 www.wildernessunion.com/)***
