SUMMARY:Intro to Survival Skills: Shelter\, Fire and Knots
DESCRIPTION:Wilderness Union Toronto - Outdoor Adventure and Hiking Club\n
 **Please note the only way to register for this adventure is on [our websi
 te.](https://www.wildernessunion.com/survival-skills/intro-survival-skills
 )**\n**Spend a Saturday becoming someone who knows what to do.**\nJoin us 
 for a hands-on beginner day in Copeland Forest with Kyle\, a survival inst
 ructor with over a decade of experience. You'll pitch a shelter\, light a 
 fire without matches\, carve with a knife and tie the knots that hold it a
 ll together.\nThis class is open to any adult\, member or not. Come on you
 r own or bring a friend. Most people at our classes arrive solo. Total beg
 inners are welcome: Kyle starts from zero\, and there's no hiking\, just s
 hort walks into the trees to gather wood.\n**Kit provided:** Tarps\, saws\
 , hatchets\, loaner ferro rods and knives to borrow\, plus your own tinder
  kit and a printed handout. Want your own ferro rod (+$10) or Mora knife (
 +$40) to keep? Add one when you book.\n**Getting there:** Add the bus for 
 $50 and we'll pick you up at Keele Station at 8am and drop you back around
  6pm. Or drive yourself to the P1 parking lot in Copeland Forest\, near Ho
 rseshoe Valley\, about an hour and a half north of Toronto.\nNo membership
  needed. After you book\, we'll email you the waiver to sign and your plan
  with directions\, timings and a packing list.\n**Accessibility**\nWildern
 ess Union is committed to making our adventures as accessible as possible.
  If you wish to make an accommodation request relating to a disability or 
 provide feedback\, please do so by sending an email to info@wildernessunio
 n.com\n**Highlights**\n**Put a roof over your head:** Learn to pick a good
  spot and pitch a tarp two ways\, the A-frame and the plow point\, so you 
 know how to stay dry when the weather turns.\n**Light a fire without match
 es:** Catch a ferro rod spark on fluffed jute\, build up through twigs to 
 logs\, split wood by batoning and carve feather sticks.\n**Knots\, knife w
 ork and a tripod grill:** Learn the taut-line hitch\, slip knot and bowlin
 e\, carve your own chopsticks\, spoon or spatula\, then lash a tripod and 
 grill over the fire.\n**Itinerary**\n**08:00** \\- Bus leaves Keele Statio
 n \\(if you've added it\\)\n**10:00** \\- Meet at location\\\, for a welco
 me\\\, safety talk and knife handling\n**Late morning** \\- Tarp shelters:
  the A\\-frame and the plow point\n**Lunch** \\- Bring a packed lunch and 
 eat around the fire\n**Afternoon** \\- Fire without matches: ferro rod\\\,
  jute\\\, batoning and feather sticks\n**Late afternoon** \\- Knots\\\, bu
 sh cutlery and a tripod grill\n**16:00** \\- Wrap up and head home\n**18:0
 0** \\- Bus arrives back at Keele Station\n**Event cost: $135+HST. $50 opt
 ional transport also available. Please register [here.](https://www.wilder
 nessunion.com/survival-skills/intro-survival-skills)**\n**About Wilderness
  Union**\nWilderness Union is deliberate about building an outdoors commun
 ity that connects you to the life-changing magic of the outdoors and helps
  you find your people.\nAttendance numbers on Meetup don't reflect our act
 ual event attendance - we typically have 15-20 community members at each e
 vent. Large enough that there's someone new to meet but small enough that 
 it's not overwhelming!\n***Learn more at our website [www.wildernessunion.
 com](https://www.wildernessunion.com/)***
